<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-3"><summary><span class="chapter-count">03</span><h3>Landscape Installation Service in Lakewood, CO — Every Phase, One Team</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Landscape installation is more than putting plants in the ground and rolling out sod. Done properly, it’s a sequenced process where every phase depends on the one before it — and where shortcuts in any phase create problems that show up months or years later. Grading affects drainage. Irrigation placement affects plant establishment. Hardscape base preparation affects whether a patio holds its level through a Colorado winter. Get the sequence wrong and the landscape fails, often expensively.</p>
<p>Our installation teams have spent more than a decade working in Lakewood and across Jefferson County. We know the soil conditions here — the clay-heavy profiles that drain poorly without amendment, the compaction that comes with new construction sites, the ground behaviour that affects hardscape stability through freeze-thaw seasons. We design and install around those conditions, not in spite of them.</p>
<p>As a full-service landscape installation contractor in Lakewood, we manage the complete scope in-house: site assessment and grading, soil preparation and amendment, irrigation system design and installation, turf laying or seeding, planting bed establishment, hardscape integration, and final site cleanup. Every phase is handled by our crew. The project doesn’t stall waiting on a subcontractor, and accountability doesn’t get lost in the handoff between a designer and a separate build team.</p>
<p>When we complete a Lakewood landscape installation, the job is finished and the landscape is ready to establish.</p>

<h3> Full Service Landscape Design in Lakewood for Every Property and Budget</h3>

<p>Lakewood is a city with genuine variety in its residential landscape — older neighbourhoods near Belmar and Lakewood Heritage Center with established trees and compact lots that need designs working sensitively with existing character, and newer developments further west with open yards that need structure, definition, and planting to feel like finished spaces.</p>
<p>Full service landscape design means we do more than hand you a drawing and wish you well. We design with installation in mind — plant selections chosen for Colorado’s climate zone and the specific conditions of your site, hardscape elements specified to hold up through freeze-thaw cycles, irrigation systems sized correctly for each zone. The design and the installation come from the same team, so the transition from plan to finished landscape is seamless.</p>
<p>We work with Lakewood homeowners across a range of project scales and budgets. Smaller properties get edited, intelligent designs that maximise what the space can do without overcomplicating it. Larger lots get landscape plans that create genuine structure — defined outdoor living zones, transition planting, feature elements, and lawn areas that work together as a cohesive whole rather than a collection of unrelated decisions.</p>
<p>We also offer phased installation for homeowners who want to complete their landscape in stages. We design the full picture upfront — so every phase builds toward a planned outcome — and install it in agreed stages that fit your schedule and budget.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-4"><summary><span class="chapter-count">04</span><h3>Commercial Landscaping Services in Lakewood for Properties That Work as Hard as You Do</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Commercial landscaping in Lakewood isn’t a cosmetic consideration — it’s a business decision. The exterior of a commercial property communicates something to every customer, tenant, and visitor before they walk through the door. A well-designed, professionally installed landscape signals that the business inside is well-run. A neglected or poorly designed one signals the opposite, and in Lakewood’s competitive commercial environment, that impression matters.</p>
<p>Ridgewell provides commercial landscaping services in Lakewood for businesses, property managers, HOAs, and commercial developers who need a landscape that looks intentional, performs through Colorado’s seasons, and is practical to manage long-term. We work on the design and installation phase — not ongoing maintenance contracts — which means our focus is entirely on getting the build right so the property performs well from day one.</p>
<p>Our commercial landscape designs are built around operational realities. Plant selections prioritise low maintenance burden and proven durability in Colorado’s climate. Irrigation systems are zoned and specified for efficiency — minimising ongoing adjustment and water waste. Hardscape elements — entry features, pathways, defined commercial planting zones — are built for high foot traffic and long-term appearance, not just initial presentation.</p>
<p>We understand that commercial projects in Lakewood have tighter timelines, more stakeholders, and site access constraints that residential projects don’t. Our process accommodates all of it — clear project scoping from the start, direct communication throughout, and installations scheduled to minimise disruption to your business operations.</p>
</div>
</details>
